00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:10.640
Of the like three modes of this game, this being the dog fighting, this was the easiest mode

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:16.800
for me to consistently win on because it's maybe a little more forgiving as long as you,

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:22.660
you know, stay behind your enemies and don't let them lock onto you and get in front of you,

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:24.520
which there's ways to get around of as well.

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:30.560
But I, I, I really do think that because it's a circular 3d space that you can, um,

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:34.800
that you can fight inside of, you're not like in, uh, in Top Gun.

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:39.480
It was kind of like, they were always just coming at you and you had to, uh, fight them that way.

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:46.460
This has a, uh, uh, sorry for people who play better fight sims, flight sims than me, but, uh,

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:51.960
Star Fox 64 has these on rail segments and then opens up to this all range mode,

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:58.880
which basically is you and the boss going in like a similar circular pattern where if you go too far,

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:00.160
you just have to be turned around.

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:04.600
And so there's this area where you have to like, think about, well, we're in like a ring

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:05.860
and we can't leave the ring.

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:08.380
So how do I best approach on my enemies?

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:13.900
And it's very similar here, uh, in Flight of the Intruder where once you pass by the enemies,

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:16.700
you have to think about, well, what's the best way to get back to them quickly?

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:22.020
Because you don't want to keep doing these long roundabouts of waiting for them to come back on

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.540
because that will take a very long time.

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:27.640
And that section does, doesn't really like evolve too much throughout the game.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.240
Yeah, I think it doesn't maybe some more enemies.

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:33.400
Like at first it's just two enemies on the screen at any given time.

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:35.420
I think they add more throughout the game.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:36.920
But that's really it.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:44.200
But even so, I would say, and maybe this speaks more to how the other modes are than, uh,

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:47.080
any positive about that mode specifically.

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:53.880
But it does feel like the most game, like complete, like actual meat of the game.

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:55.200
Like that is the meat of the game.

00:17:55.540 --> 00:18:00.940
Yeah, I guess like the most interesting thing that happens in, in the, uh, later levels of the game,

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:05.360
and this happens in all three modes as well, is that some missions have to take place at night.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:12.080
And so then everything is like darker and maybe a little bit harder to read, uh, you know, your enemies and everything.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.600
That's kind of subjective.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.300
It's just different colors.

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:18.680
But I, you know, I appreciate them trying something different there nevertheless.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:23.600
And, uh, yes, the enemies, uh, become, they've become a lot more of them.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:30.980
And I'm not implying that it's easy to, uh, dodge everything that they're throwing at you as, as they're attacking you.

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:36.780
But it is the kind of thing that like, as long as you can approach your enemies and kind of take them down one by one,

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:39.460
rather than trying to like, you know, hit three in a row or something.

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:43.200
Uh, you know, that's how this kind of fighting is rewarded in the game.

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:48.440
I do like the, at least the visual variety of the night missions.

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:53.540
I mean, it is basically just like when you plugged an original Game Boy game into a Game Boy Color,

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:58.780
and then you could, uh, like do those button combinations to change the color palette.

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:04.540
Like it's basically that, but it does at least make it feel, it does feel like you're at night now.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:11.780
That's fun. And then the second mode introduced in the game after you successfully, uh, do the dog fighting

00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:13.580
is this bombing view.

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:18.620
Uh, the camera sits behind the plane, um, and you steer the plane left to right.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:23.020
And you have your, uh, you fire, uh, both missiles to the ground.

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:25.140
And there are these radar guided missiles.

00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:33.040
This one I struggled with a little bit because I couldn't tell if I was just running out of these radar guided missiles.

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:37.220
But once you don't have the ones that lock on and hit these ships automatically,

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:45.100
it was really hard to tell where these air to ground missiles were going to like make contact with,

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:47.600
with the opposing ships.

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:53.280
So I started to like reliably blow stuff up early on and then just get worse and worse.

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:58.400
And that's not great because there is, um, you know, your, uh, what is it?

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:03.060
Your DEFCON is going down as you, uh, so you started like DEFCON five.

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:06.780
And then as you missed each target, it counts down until it goes to zero.

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:14.140
And so it doesn't take very long, uh, to get to zero once you, if you, if you can't use the air to ground missiles successfully.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:22.680
Yeah. It was like a weird like shmup, but not shmup because you're not shooting at things like directly in front of you.

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:24.760
And I know we've had shmups where you're shooting at ground.

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:27.100
You could shoot at things on the ground and in the air.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:34.500
But like, yeah, like you said, it, it's hard to, you can't like aim directly at the thing that, you know,

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:37.920
the thing you're trying to hit does not go into the center of your crosshairs.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:43.140
When you fire, you have to kind of like intuit a little bit where the bomb will fall.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:47.080
And I think visually that's really cool.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:52.560
I think that the, this, this, this level, I think is one of the cooler ones visually in this game.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:54.200
One of the cooler ones of the three.

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:56.940
Um, but,

00:20:57.100 --> 00:21:01.120
I do, I do think it is pretty cool visually because it does kind of give you like, yeah,

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:06.960
I've never flown a bomber plane before, but it gives you the vibe of like what you see in the movies where it's like,

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:11.140
if you're, if they're bombing some, like a boat in the water, it's like there's,

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:13.720
there's three misses before there's a hit as they fly over.

00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:18.560
And it kind of like was reminiscent of like that, that visual to me.

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:24.620
Um, but yeah, gameplay, actual game feel wise, it, it, it took a lot of getting used to.

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:27.400
Yeah. You do run out of the missiles.

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:39.140
Um, and you do have some control over like the trajectory of your regular old, like dumb mission missiles,

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:45.200
or I don't even know bombs, machine gun fire, whatever those projectiles are.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:48.780
Um, but so, but yeah, you do have to kind of lead them.

00:21:49.020 --> 00:21:58.740
I kind of just like would spam a bunch of, I would kind of vary how high or low of a trajectory.

00:21:59.180 --> 00:22:04.320
And I would just kind of like spam the fire button and that, that usually worked.

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:12.300
But yeah, you do, once you let enough go, you do end up in a, uh, uh, kind of a, a mess.

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:16.640
Like where they just shoot a bunch of missiles at you and you kind of got to dance around.

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:25.360
I did like the kind of like dodging mechanics where if you kind of, you kind of angle up and you, when you're up there,

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:31.880
you have a bit more, uh, like lateral control so that you can dodge the stuff that they're firing at you.

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:38.340
But it's also easy to lose track of the fire coming your way.

00:22:38.720 --> 00:22:46.980
Um, when you're kind of like, you're trying so hard just to like lead these bombs in, on the right course.

00:22:47.400 --> 00:22:51.740
Um, it's, it's, it's still got, it's got some mechanics to it.

00:22:51.820 --> 00:23:00.320
It's not as simple as just like a regular old shmup thing, like Joe was saying, but, um, uh, still, still feels very much like a mini game.

00:23:00.320 --> 00:23:03.360
Broken down to its like simplest, uh, description.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:12.160
It's kind of just like space invaders or, uh, centipede, you know, it's just like these, these targets are coming towards the set, you know, closer to your side of the screen.

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:15.900
And you have to target them before they, uh, before they cross you.

00:23:16.300 --> 00:23:27.180
But the added element of dodging their fire while you're trying to fire is the most interesting part or rather the most engaging part of the gameplay.

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:38.520
Because if you were just sitting pretty and just trying to like knock out as many of these things as you can and that affected score or, uh, the following mission or something, it would be kind of trivial in the grand scheme of things.

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:49.500
But having to dodge their bullets and especially as you, uh, start, uh, not being able to reliably take these turrets out, uh, there's a lot to dodge on screen.

00:23:50.020 --> 00:23:55.520
And, uh, the air, I'm sold on this, like the view that we get of the airplane.

00:23:55.520 --> 00:23:59.060
Like I love all looking at all the different like twists and turns.

00:23:59.260 --> 00:24:01.140
I do all the alternate angles they got.

00:24:01.480 --> 00:24:13.160
Uh, these sprites are, are great to look at of the plane and I buy all of its twisty turning still with just this horizon line and, uh, the water rapids like flowing at you.

00:24:13.160 --> 00:24:26.280
I think it's funny that like, you know, there's, there's, there's the ocean levels, um, where you're doing that over water and the things you're trying to hit are very clearly like battleships and carriers.

00:24:26.740 --> 00:24:34.540
Um, but then there's, uh, the same kind of, you know, scrolling, not so shmup over land.

00:24:35.360 --> 00:24:39.420
And there's some stuff that like, Oh, you can tell like, that's probably a tank.

00:24:39.420 --> 00:24:43.280
Like, Oh, that's, that's like an artillery battery or something.

00:24:43.500 --> 00:24:46.100
But then there's some that are like, is that a village?

00:24:46.300 --> 00:24:48.500
Like, am I, am I bombing a village?

00:24:49.460 --> 00:24:51.120
Yeah. I think it might be a hangar.

00:24:52.080 --> 00:24:52.920
Residential houses.

00:24:53.300 --> 00:24:54.520
It looks like. Yeah.

00:24:55.460 --> 00:24:59.120
What was the other game we played where we were like taking out entire neighborhoods?

00:25:00.280 --> 00:25:01.940
Oh yeah. It was like a shmup.

00:25:02.100 --> 00:25:07.340
We were like flying into like, that was the one where we were, um, we were like a floating head, right?

00:25:07.920 --> 00:25:10.000
Hmm. I thought we were a plane or something.

00:25:10.240 --> 00:25:13.780
Oh, I'm thinking of that crazy one that we just played like earlier this year.

00:25:14.300 --> 00:25:15.660
Zombie nation. Oh yeah.

00:25:15.760 --> 00:25:21.680
I know. Zombie nation. The one where it was like, everybody's been turned into zombies and you're this floating head and you just had to destroy skyscrapers.

00:25:22.320 --> 00:25:23.420
Oh yes. Zombies?

00:25:23.840 --> 00:25:25.500
No, you weren't a zombie.

00:25:25.660 --> 00:25:26.840
Everybody else was zombie.

00:25:27.420 --> 00:25:29.740
Okay. This is just a classic case of Sean.

00:25:29.740 --> 00:25:31.380
I can't believe you wouldn't remember that.

00:25:31.540 --> 00:25:38.700
I just Googled. I Googled shmup where you are in a neighborhood NES and the AI overview said.

00:25:38.720 --> 00:25:39.940
I can't believe it wasn't.

00:25:39.940 --> 00:25:40.880
That's not what I'm thinking.

00:25:40.900 --> 00:25:43.960
I thought it was Mr. Rogers, uh, shmup simulator.

00:25:45.280 --> 00:25:46.820
Show me what you got simulator.

00:25:48.060 --> 00:25:50.200
Uh, Sean, you definitely remember zombie nation.

00:25:50.200 --> 00:25:57.120
Take a look at that while we talk about the next, the next possible thing we could talk about, which is the third part of each one of these missions.

00:25:57.440 --> 00:26:02.420
Uh, just like in any, uh, any good flight sim, eventually you have to land the plane.

00:26:02.600 --> 00:26:05.060
Uh, and that is exactly what you have to do here.

00:26:05.760 --> 00:26:13.540
I, I don't know if I held this point of view in, uh, Top Gun or other, uh, flight sims where we have to land.

00:26:13.900 --> 00:26:19.560
But for some reason in this one, I was fine with, with dying a lot.

00:26:19.580 --> 00:26:22.500
And it was fun, like learning what was going on.

00:26:22.620 --> 00:26:24.380
And I thought you were gonna say you used to.

00:26:24.520 --> 00:26:25.640
No, no, it's not easy at all.

00:26:25.700 --> 00:26:29.920
But I was kind of fine with it and being like, ah, okay, I just needed to, I need to come down a little earlier.

00:26:30.100 --> 00:26:31.520
I just needed to slow down a little bit.

00:26:31.540 --> 00:26:36.820
It's like, I never quite figured out exactly what I was doing wrong, but it always just felt like I was temporarily embarrassed.

00:26:37.060 --> 00:26:39.640
And the next attempt would certainly fix it.

00:26:40.860 --> 00:26:49.160
I was okay to try, but I'll tell you why I wasn't okay with like, with just the, the, the way that they present this.

00:26:49.480 --> 00:26:55.580
Like it's, I know that this is a very difficult thing to do to land on an aircraft carrier in real life.

00:26:55.920 --> 00:27:02.380
Very difficult. But the thing that you have in, when you're in an aircraft is that you can see the aircraft carrier.

00:27:02.820 --> 00:27:09.420
And in this, like, I'm sure that while you're landing, you're, you're landing a plane, you have to look at a lot of numbers and stuff.

00:27:09.420 --> 00:27:10.580
On your, on your display.

00:27:11.480 --> 00:27:19.980
But this, it's all I have is this tiny little, these tiny little readout of numbers at the top left corner that like, yeah, my brain, I can look at it and think about it.

00:27:20.040 --> 00:27:25.260
But like, my brain doesn't interpret that as much as my brain interprets a big massive boat coming at me.

00:27:25.420 --> 00:27:27.580
It's like, it doesn't interpret that as quickly.

00:27:27.580 --> 00:27:38.800
So like, it's, it's like, it's just like an extra step of like translation in my head to figure out how close I am to this aircraft carrier, how close I am to the ground and the speed I'm going and all these things.

00:27:38.800 --> 00:27:56.280
It just feels like I kind of wish that they maybe figured out a way to do this in first person or to like somehow show me a, a, uh, like a readout, like a, like a radar thing of like me, the aircraft carrier.

00:27:56.280 --> 00:28:01.100
So I can see a visual indication of how close I'm getting rather than like a number readout.

00:28:01.820 --> 00:28:02.840
Um, okay.

00:28:02.860 --> 00:28:06.940
So I, I, I was okay at the landing.

00:28:06.940 --> 00:28:13.200
I think maybe I was okay at the landing in, um, the, uh, what was it?

00:28:13.340 --> 00:28:14.540
Top gun as well.

00:28:14.540 --> 00:28:17.820
So, um, you, you, you guys crashed a lot.

00:28:17.920 --> 00:28:19.260
I crashed it at first.

00:28:19.760 --> 00:28:22.280
Did, did, did you guys, did you guys ever get the hang of it?

00:28:22.780 --> 00:28:28.180
I think I landed like once or twice and I couldn't, I couldn't recreate it afterwards.

00:28:28.620 --> 00:28:31.700
I don't know. I was very bad at it is I was like, Oh, I did it.

00:28:31.800 --> 00:28:32.700
All right. Now I know what I'm doing.

00:28:32.760 --> 00:28:34.300
And then I would just crash another 30 times.

00:28:34.380 --> 00:28:36.300
And I kind of came around. I got the hang of it.

00:28:36.460 --> 00:28:43.400
Once I realized that I'm sure this is in the manual, that the aircraft carrier does not change height.

00:28:43.400 --> 00:28:47.940
Uh, you don't go to different aircraft carriers or they don't like sporadically change between the levels.

00:28:48.080 --> 00:28:52.180
The aircraft carriers altitude is always going to be at 70 feet.

00:28:52.440 --> 00:29:00.820
So you basically just have to come down enough so that you're in like the, you know, 80 to 100 range.

00:29:00.980 --> 00:29:06.620
And then find your way to like adjust your thrusters just enough to hang there.

00:29:06.760 --> 00:29:10.520
And then you can focus on range and be like, okay, it's coming, it's coming.

00:29:10.520 --> 00:29:14.740
And then slow down progressively until you land on the aircraft carrier.

00:29:15.300 --> 00:29:17.300
The, the, it's, it's not a helicarrier.

00:29:17.460 --> 00:29:23.200
The, the, the trick, the trick here, of course, is that, uh, the range changes every time.

00:29:23.360 --> 00:29:25.300
So sometimes you have significantly less time.

00:29:25.480 --> 00:29:26.920
Other times you have a lot more time.

00:29:27.540 --> 00:29:34.180
Um, and you also have to do this extra added element of, and what is that?

00:29:34.280 --> 00:29:35.140
Or is that an anchor?

00:29:35.140 --> 00:29:40.300
Like is, you, you're, you have to, the flight, the landing gear?

00:29:40.300 --> 00:29:41.320
No, no, the thing in the back.

00:29:41.480 --> 00:29:43.400
No, after that, once you've landed.

00:29:44.540 --> 00:29:49.720
Oh, yeah. I think that's like, yeah, it's kind of, maybe anchor's the wrong word, but it's like a hook.

00:29:49.720 --> 00:29:55.080
And so you have to also press a button for that too, to, um, to have that come out.

00:29:55.080 --> 00:30:00.180
And so that that can help you stop because you, if you don't, you could just risk going

00:30:00.180 --> 00:30:02.560
right off the carrier even after you've landed.

00:30:03.400 --> 00:30:04.380
Which is fun.

00:30:04.580 --> 00:30:05.840
Take right off again.

00:30:06.080 --> 00:30:09.240
Just, yeah. I don't understand why it's punishment to just keep going.

00:30:09.860 --> 00:30:12.200
Who do, they didn't think I was going to just turn around?

00:30:12.500 --> 00:30:14.680
Playing the game more is punishment for that?

00:30:14.680 --> 00:30:19.280
Yeah, that's, it's like, it basically, the whole thing is, and I feel like this is the

00:30:19.280 --> 00:30:24.760
second comparison of Flappy Bird that I've made in, uh, however many weeks, but it's

00:30:24.760 --> 00:30:29.700
just like a very, uh, drawn out version of Flappy Bird.

00:30:29.900 --> 00:30:37.900
Like, like matching the, the thrust to like your vertical altitude, vertical velocity or

00:30:37.900 --> 00:30:43.860
whatever. Um, you know, once, once you get that, that kind of stable, you're, you're all good.

00:30:44.300 --> 00:30:48.840
Joe, I did feel like you though, that it, it was kind of surprising that on a simulation

00:30:48.840 --> 00:30:51.620
level, they wouldn't try to do this in the first person.

00:30:51.960 --> 00:30:54.380
Yeah. And I don't know, was Top Gun?

00:30:54.980 --> 00:30:57.880
No, no. No, that was from the side as well.

00:30:58.100 --> 00:31:03.400
It was, yeah. I'm sure it's actually like really difficult to do that in, because of the way these first

00:31:03.400 --> 00:31:04.340
person levels work.

00:31:04.520 --> 00:31:07.580
It's like, how do you, how do you show getting closer to the ground?

00:31:07.740 --> 00:31:13.780
How do you show like, I don't know, there's probably a lot more robust elements you need to

00:31:13.780 --> 00:31:19.760
include than just a solid blue mat and a solid dark blue mat, you know, to do that.

00:31:19.860 --> 00:31:21.460
But like, I wish that they could.

00:31:21.700 --> 00:31:25.120
And, and I think that, you know, this is maybe me getting ahead of myself, but like the, I

00:31:25.120 --> 00:31:29.340
think the biggest takeaway I had from this game in general and in, in all games like

00:31:29.340 --> 00:31:35.600
this is that, uh, they, I think that like, they, they have this really cool thing of being

00:31:35.600 --> 00:31:39.680
very like simulation focused, uh, flight games.

00:31:39.860 --> 00:31:41.540
And I just don't think the technology is there.

00:31:41.680 --> 00:31:43.860
I don't think the technology is there to do it.

00:31:43.920 --> 00:31:49.740
And I think that's why I always like feel that they, like, they just don't hit exactly

00:31:49.740 --> 00:31:51.300
the way that they're trying to when I play.

00:31:51.300 --> 00:31:56.480
I mean, what the computer game is doing is even crazier because that one has like, you

00:31:56.480 --> 00:32:01.900
actually have to like make your way out to the missions and have to like plan with your

00:32:01.900 --> 00:32:02.800
compass and shit.

00:32:03.040 --> 00:32:07.280
Like, you know, okay, I've got to fly for like, it's like elite dangerous for, right.

00:32:07.420 --> 00:32:11.900
I've got to like fly three minutes Northwest and then, uh, you know, adjust my compass to

00:32:11.900 --> 00:32:14.620
go East. And then I fly seven minutes in that direction.

00:32:14.760 --> 00:32:17.700
And I should be, cause you know, there's no like GPS or anything.

00:32:17.700 --> 00:32:20.320
And then you just like, yep, I arrived at the, at the fight.

00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:24.580
It's kind of nuts, but like, thank goodness they took that part of the game.

00:32:24.680 --> 00:32:27.440
I'm sure they just couldn't fit it on the cartridge, but like, thank goodness that's

00:32:27.440 --> 00:32:31.700
out. And you just get dropped right into the dog fights, uh, because there's a lot more.

00:32:31.700 --> 00:32:37.720
